			<div class="content" id="post-content-2753629">
									

<p>Well. While I would love to upvote given the overhaul on the first document alone, there's still a number of problems keeping me from doing so.</p>
<p>First, I still feel like the abilities of doc1 are too different from the abilities in -2. I think it would have been more logical for them to be -2's abilities perception-shifted into a MPATHG context. This goes double for the interview. I think going out of your way to tailor the -1 portion into a 'veiled by cognitohazard' version of the actuality of -2 would have made the reveal that much more satisfying.</p>
<p>Second, I think the second document's effects are oddly complicated: So, he sees potential weapons as safe items, but at the same time, sees them as being harmful, and still attempts to attack people with them? How exactly do knives take on the weight and texture of a cushion, still remain physically the same, yet not be harmful if you assault someone with it? I guess it's part of the joke, but the description of his effects seems weird.</p>
<p>Third, and this is my biggest gripe of all, the second interview. I'm just so damn disinterested in this skip's wistful memories of his creators and how lovingly thoughtful they are; and over-explaining the joke. I feel like it does nothing but reiterate for the umpteenth flipping time: 'gee, aren't these GAW guys just so sincere and funny? They sure do funny things because humor is something they get. You like humor and jokes, yes? You'll like them. Why, they are just like you and me.'. Christ, just no. The whole thing grinds to a screeching halt here.</p>

